// Demonstrating Declarable Modules & Class Keyword Overrides

// 1. Declarable Modules
Joe establishes MathHelper:
    Joe remembers multiplier as 3.

    To triple with x:
        Joe delivers x * multiplier.
    That's how Joe does it.
That's MathHelper.

Joe yells "Tripling 7 yields: " + MathHelper.triple(7).

// 2. Class Keyword Overriding (Yell & Whisper to custom targets)
Meet a CustomLogger:
    It has prefix.

    To yell with msg:
        Joe yells "📢 [" + jthis.prefix + "] " + msg.
    That's how Joe does it.

    To whisper with msg:
        Joe yells "🤫 [" + jthis.prefix + " (quiet)] " + msg.
    That's how Joe does it.
That's a CustomLogger.

Joe remembers my_log as a new CustomLogger("SYSTEM").
Joe yells "Important broadcast!" to my_log.
Joe whispers "Internal diagnostic" to my_log.

// 3. Yelling and Whispering directly to files
Joe yells "Log entry from Joe" to "examples_run.log".
Joe whispers " — appended data" to "examples_run.log".

Joe yells "Successfully demonstrated declarable modules and keyword overrides!".
